{"id": "EUVD-2026-97050", "enisaUuid": "a8216557-5cce-3ead-a1ec-4a6c996df289", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the putCancelQuit handler of SysUserController, allowing any authenticated user to cancel user resignations. Low-privileged attackers can supply user ids and a tenantId parameter or X-Tenant-Id header to restore ended, pending, or refused tenant memberships to normal.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:33:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:51:16", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_sys_user_cancel_quit.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysUserController.java#L1867-L1877", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-user-putcancelquit"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108876", "GHSA-pmhm-r7h7-cxvj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "22cc759b-38a9-30f3-9cab-d68a79effc50", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "97590bb4-38a7-35ba-8490-89aa72e4346e", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}